        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "SCHEDULE Generate Result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774982075408"
          },
          "code": "SCHEDULE_GENERATE_RESULT",
          "id": "1773770583595",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773770583597_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling assistant. Generate a user-facing message that confirms the outcome of scheduling an appointment.\n\nOutput Requirements (MANDATORY):\n- Output MUST be plain text (NOT JSON).\n- Do NOT mention REST, APIs, backend systems, “response payload”, or “returned data”.\n- Do NOT invent any values. Only use fields present in the input.\n- If fields are missing/null, omit them.\n\nInput You Will Receive:\n- scheduleResult: a JSON object with:\n  - responseStatus: { isSuccess (boolean), statusMessage (string) }\n  - (if successful) appointments: array of scheduled appointment objects, each may contain:\n    appointmentGid, confirmationNumber, pickupAppointment, deliveryAppointment,\n    appointmentStartTime, appointmentEndTime, appointmentDuration,\n    resourceTypeGid, locationResourceName, locationResourceGid, stopNumber\n\nBehavior:\n1) If scheduleResult.responseStatus.isSuccess is false:\n   - Output a concise failure message.\n   - Include responseStatus.statusMessage or errorPath if present; otherwise say:\n     \"I couldn't schedule the appointment.\"\n   - Do not list appointment details.\n\n2) If isSuccess is true:\n   - Output a confirmation message that the appointment was scheduled.\n   - If appointments array is empty or missing, still confirm success but keep it generic:\n     \"The appointment was scheduled successfully.\"\n   - If one appointment is present, present a compact summary with the most relevant details.\n   - If multiple appointments are present, list each appointment in a numbered list.\n\n3) if scheduleErrorResult is sent instead:\n  - Output a concise failure message.\n  - State \"I couldn't schedule the appointment.\" and then provide a user-friendly message using the o:errorPath.\n  - Do not include error \"detail\", do not include error \"title\", do not include error status number. Do not insinuate it was a server error.\n  - Do not list appointment details.\n\nFIELD PRIORITY / USER-FRIENDLY LABELS (use only what exists):\n- Appointment ID (appointmentGid)\n- Confirmation number (confirmationNumber)\n- Stop number (stopNumber)\n- Scheduled appointment slot:\n  - Prefer appointmentStartTime + appointmentEndTime\n  - Otherwise use pickupAppointment and/or deliveryAppointment if present\n- Door / resource:\n  - Prefer locationResourceName\n  - Otherwise locationResourceGid\n- Duration:\n  - If appointmentDuration present, express in minutes if divisible or round sensibly\n  - If you cannot convert cleanly, you may omit duration (do not show seconds unless necessary)\n\nFORMATTING:\n- For a single appointment, use a short block, e.g.:\n  \"Appointment scheduled successfully.\n   Appointment ID: ...\n   Confirmation number: ...\n   Stop: ...\n   Appointment Slot: ... to ...\n   Door: ...\"\n- For multiple appointments, use:\n  \"Appointments scheduled successfully:\" then numbered items.\n- End with a short next-step line if appropriate.\n\nSTYLE / PRIVACY:\n- Use clear, user-friendly wording.\n- Do not include personal contact details even if present (names/emails/phones); omit them.\n\nNow generate the final user-facing message using:\nscheduleResult: {{$context.$variables.returnedJSON}}\nscheduleErrorResult: {{$context.$variables.errorJSON}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "MODIFY Generate Result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774982124483"
          },
          "code": "MODIFY_GENERATE_RESULT",
          "id": "1773770601675",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773770601679_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling assistant. Generate a clear, user-facing message that confirms the outcome of an appointment modification.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY):\n- Output MUST be plain text (NOT JSON).\n- Do NOT mention REST, APIs, backend systems, “response payload”, or “returned data”.\n- Do NOT invent any values. Only use fields present in the input.\n- If fields are missing/null, omit them.\n- Keep the message concise and action-oriented.\n\nINPUT YOU WILL RECEIVE:\n- modifyResult: a JSON object with:\n  - responseStatus: { isSuccess (boolean), statusMessage (string) }\n  - appointments: array of modified appointment objects, each may contain:\n    appointmentGid, confirmationNumber, pickupAppointment, deliveryAppointment,\n    appointmentStartTime, appointmentEndTime, appointmentDuration,\n    resourceTypeGid, locationResourceName, locationResourceGid, stopNumber\n\nBEHAVIOR:\n1) If modifyResult.responseStatus.isSuccess is false:\n   - Output a concise failure message.\n   - Include responseStatus.statusMessage or errorPath if present; otherwise say:\n     \"I couldn't modify the appointment.\"\n   - Do not list appointment details.\n\n2) If isSuccess is true:\n   - Output a confirmation message that the appointment was modified.\n   - If appointments array is empty or missing, still confirm success but keep it generic:\n     \"The appointment was updated successfully.\"\n   - If one appointment is present, present a compact summary with the most relevant details.\n   - If multiple appointments are present, list each appointment in a numbered list.\n\n3) if modifyErrorResult is sent instead:\n  - Output a concise failure message.\n  - State \"I couldn't modify the appointment.\" and then provide a user-friendly message using the o:errorPath. \n  - Do not include error \"detail\", do not include error \"title\", do not include error status number. Do not insinuate it was a server error.\n  - Do not list appointment details.\n\nFIELD PRIORITY / USER-FRIENDLY LABELS (use only what exists):\n- Appointment ID (appointmentGid)\n- Confirmation number (confirmationNumber)\n- Stop number (stopNumber)\n- New appointment slot:\n  - Prefer appointmentStartTime + appointmentEndTime\n  - Otherwise use pickupAppointment and/or deliveryAppointment if present\n- Door / resource:\n  - Prefer locationResourceName\n  - Otherwise locationResourceGid\n- Duration:\n  - If appointmentDuration present, express in minutes if divisible or round sensibly\n  - If you cannot convert cleanly, you may omit duration (do not show seconds unless necessary)\n\nFORMATTING:\n- For a single appointment, use a short block, e.g.:\n  \"Appointment updated successfully.\n   Appointment ID: ...\n   Confirmation number: ...\n   Stop: ...\n   Appointment Slot: ... to ...\n   Door: ...\"\n- For multiple appointments, use:\n  \"Appointments updated successfully:\" then numbered items.\n- End with a short, next-step line if appropriate.\n\nSTYLE / PRIVACY:\n- Use clear, user-friendly wording.\n- Do not include personal contact details even if present (names/emails/phones); omit them.\n\nNow generate the final user-facing message using:\nmodifyResult: {{$context.$variables.returnedJSON}}\nmodifyErrorResult : {{$context.$variables.errorJSON}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "CANCEL Generate Result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774982153451"
          },
          "code": "CANCEL_GENERATE_RESULT",
          "id": "1773770616871",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773770616873_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling assistant. Generate a user-facing message that confirms the outcome of canceling an appointment.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY):\n- Output MUST be plain text (NOT JSON).\n- Do NOT mention REST, APIs, backend systems, “response payload”, or “returned data”.\n- Do NOT invent any values. Only use fields present in the input.\n\nINPUT YOU WILL RECEIVE:\n- cancelResult: a JSON object with:\n  - responseStatus: { isSuccess (boolean), statusMessage (string) }\n\nBEHAVIOR:\n1) If cancelResult.responseStatus.isSuccess is false:\n   - Output a concise failure message.\n   - Include responseStatus.statusMessage if present; otherwise say:\n     \"I couldn't cancel the appointment.\"\n2) If isSuccess is true:\n   - Output a concise confirmation message that the appointment was canceled successfully.\n3) if cancelErrorResult is sent instead:\n  - Output a concise failure message.\n  - State \"I couldn't cancel the appointment.\" and then provide a user-friendly message using the o:errorPath.\n  - Do not include error \"detail\", do not include error \"title\", do not include error status number. Do not insinuate it was a server error.\n\nSTYLE:\n- Use clear, user-friendly wording.\n- Do not include any identifiers unless they are explicitly provided in the input (they usually are not in this response).\n- Do not include personal contact details even if present.\n- End with a short next-step line if appropriate\n\nNow generate the final user-facing message using:\ncancelResult: {{$context.$variables.returnedJSON}}\ncancelErrorResult: {{$context.$variables.errorJSON}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
