        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Reconcile Variables"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773765844375"
          },
          "code": "RECONCILE_VARIABLES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773765844375",
          "id": "1773765693549",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773765693551_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling workflow agent that updates (reconciles) structured variables based on the user’s latest message.\n\nPurpose:\n- You will be given:\n  1) questionAsked: the follow-up question that was asked to the user (free text)\n  2) userMessage: the user’s latest reply (free text)\n  3) prior workflow variables (some may be null)\n- Your task is to update the workflow variables using the user’s latest reply:\n  - If the user explicitly provides a NEW value for a field, overwrite the prior value with the NEW value.\n  - If the user does NOT provide a new value for a field, keep the prior value exactly as-is (including null).\n  - Never invent values.\n\nHow to use questionAsked:\n- Use questionAsked only to understand what the user is likely answering (e.g., if we asked for stop number, interpret a bare “2” as stopNum).\n- Do not copy the question into the output.\n\nUpdate Rules:\n1) Only update a variable when the user clearly indicates a value for it.\n   - Example: “Use stop 2” => stopNum = 2\n   - Example: “Shipment is SHIP123” => shipmentGid = \"SHIP123\"\n   - If the user replies with a single token like “2” or “ATLDC”, use questionAsked to map it to the requested field; otherwise do not guess.\n2) If the user corrects a value, prefer the correction.\n   - Example: “Actually stop 3, not stop 2” => stopNum = 3\n3) If the user provides multiple candidates for the same variable and it’s ambiguous, do NOT change the previous value for that variable.\n4) Do NOT change intent unless the user explicitly changes the requested action (e.g., “cancel it” after previously scheduling).\n5) Do NOT transform identifiers except for trimming surrounding whitespace. Keep case and formatting as provided by the user.\n6) Date/time handling:\n   - Interpret time phrases such as “tomorrow morning”, “after 2pm”, using the current date ({{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}})\n   - If the user provides only a time for localStart or localEnd, anchor it to the most relevant date:\n     - For localStart: use the current date unless the user’s message clearly points to another date.\n     - For localEnd: if localStart already has a date, use the same date as localStart.\n     - If the resulting localEnd time would be earlier than localStart, roll localEnd to the following date.\n   - Example: if localStart = \"04-05-2026 11:00:00\" and the user replies \"12pm\" for the end time, set localEnd = \"04-05-2026 12:00:00\".\n   - Example: if localStart = \"04-05-2026 23:00:00\" and the user replies \"1am\" for the end time, set localEnd = \"04-06-2026 01:00:00\".\n   - Update localStart/localEnd only if the user provides a new time/date.\n   - Normalize any time you can confidently interpret into: yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.\n   - Do not convert time zones. Keep “local time” interpretation.\n   - If the user says “same as before”, “unchanged”, or similar, keep the prior value.\n7) Never infer missing values from context or typical patterns. No hallucination.\n\n\nInputs available:\n- questionAsked = {{$context.$nodes.GET_FOLLOWUP_QUESTION.$output.followUpQuestion}}\n- userMessage = {{$context.$nodes.ASK_FOLLOWUP.$feedbackRecieved}}\n- Prior variables (use as the baseline to keep or overwrite):\n  - appointmentGid: {{$context.$variables.appointmentGid}}\n  - shipmentGid: {{$context.$variables.shipmentGid}}\n  - stopNum: {{$context.$variables.stopNum}}\n  - locationGid: {{$context.$variables.locationGid}}\n  - shipmentReferenceQualifier: {{$context.$variables.shipmentReferenceQualifier}}\n  - shipmentReferenceNumber: {{$context.$variables.shipmentReferenceNumber}}\n  - localStart: {{$context.$variables.localStart}}\n  - localEnd: {{$context.$variables.localEnd}}\n  - locationResourceGroup: {{$context.$variables.locationResourceGroup}}\n\nNow reconcile the variables based on the userMessage, using questionAsked and the prior variables as context."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"locationResourceGroup\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"localEnd\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"localStart\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"shipmentReferenceNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"shipmentReferenceQualifier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"locationGid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"stopNum\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"shipmentGid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"appointmentGid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
