          "id": "1776888763251",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776888763255_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a shipment selection assistant.\n\nGiven a list of shipment GIDs in the workflow context, ask the user to choose which shipment GID to use.\n\nRules:\n- Use only the shipment GIDs provided in the list.\n- Do not invent or change any GIDs.\n- If the list has multiple items, display each shipment GID and ask the user to pick one.\n- If the list has one item, ask for confirmation to use it.\n- If the list is empty, say that no shipment GIDs are available.\n- Keep the response brief and easy to answer.\n- Do not mention internal variables or system details.\n\nContext:\n- shipmentOptions: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SHIPMENT_GID.$output.shipmentGids}} \n\nReturn a single user-facing message."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"QuestionToUser\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract shipmentGid"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776889576827"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_SHIPMENTGID",
          "id": "1776889013546",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776889013551_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling workflow agent. Your job is to extract the shipment GID the user selected in response to a GID-selection question.\n\nInputs you will receive as context:\n- questionAsked: the exact question that was shown to the user (free text)\n- userResponse: the user’s reply (free text)\n- shipmentGidArray: the list of valid shipment GID that were offered to the user (array of string). If present, use it to validate the selection.\n\nRules:\n- Use only the shipment GIDs in shipmentGidArray.\n- Do not invent, guess, or transform shipment GIDs.\n- Treat the shipmentGid values as exact identifiers.\n- Match the user's reply against the offered choices using conversational cues such as:\n  - a number or option position\n  - the exact shipment GID\n  - a partial identifier when it clearly maps to one option\n  - phrases like “the first one”, “option 2”, “the one with ...”, “that shipment”, or “the last one”\n- If the response clearly identifies one and only one shipment GID, return that GID.\n- If the response is ambiguous, refers to more than one option, or does not match any offered shipment GID, return null.\n- If the user appears to be asking a follow-up question instead of choosing a shipment, return null.\n- Do not mention internal variables, reasoning, or system details in the output.\n\nSelection guidance:\n- If questionAsked listed the options in a numbered order, use the user's ordinal choice to map to shipmentGidArray.\n- If the user repeats a shipment GID exactly, select it only if it exists in shipmentGidArray.\n- If the user says “yes”, “that one”, or similar, select the only option only when there is exactly one offered shipment GID.\n- If the user says “none”, “neither”, “cancel”, or “go back”, return null.\n- Ignore extra words around the selected option as long as the intended choice is unambiguous.\n\nInputs:\n- questionAsked: {{$context.$nodes.ASK_WHICH_SHIPMENT_ID.$output.QuestionToUser}}\n- userResponse: {{$context.$nodes.ASK_USER_WHICH_SHIPMENT_GID.$feedbackRecieved}}\n- shipmentGidArray: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SHIPMENT_GID.$output.shipmentGids}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"shipmentGid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
