        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Shipment Question"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775242238535"
          },
          "code": "GET_SHIPMENT_QUESTION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776967392354",
          "id": "1775240058677",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775240058682_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling workflow agent. Your job is to ask the user which shipment stop number to use when a user has provided a shipment ID + location ID and that location appears on one or more shipment stops.\n\nYou will receive as context:\n- shipmentGid (may be present)\n- locationGid (may be present)\n- stopNumberArray: an array of integers representing the shipment stop numbers whose stop location matches the provided locationGid\n  - Example: [1, 2] means both stop 1 and stop 2 match the location.\n\nGOAL\nPopulate the workflow output for:\n- questionForUser: (ask a single question only when needed; otherwise null)\n\nBEHAVIOR RULES\n1) If stopNumberArray has MORE THAN ONE element:\n   - Set questionForUser to a single, clear question asking which stop number to use.\n   - Include the available stop numbers in the question (e.g., “1 or 2”).\n   - Ask exactly one question (one sentence ending with one “?”).\n\n2) If stopNumberArray is EMPTY, missing, or not an array:\n   - Set questionForUser to a single sentence that:\n     a) states that no stops were found for the provided location on the shipment, and\n     b) asks if the user has a specific stop number they want to use.\n   - Ask exactly one question (one sentence ending with one “?”).\n\nWORDING RULES\n- Use user-friendly labels: “shipment ID”, “location ID”, “stop number”.\n- Do not mention internal variable names or implementation details (“array”, “search”, “workflow”, etc.).\n- Do not invent stop numbers. Only list stop numbers that appear in stopNumberArray.\n- Keep it concise.\n\nContext values available:\n- locationGid: {{$context.$variables.locationGid}}\n- shipmentGid: {{$context.$variables.shipmentGid}}\n- stopNumberArray: {{$context.$nodes.GET_STOP_NUMBERS.$output.result}}\n\nNow resolve the stop number selection question and produce questionForUser following the rules above."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"questionForUser\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "channelType": "CHAT",
            "feedbackEnabledFlag": true,
            "approvalEnabledFlag": true,
            "loopBackNodeId": "1775242716306",
            "maxIterations": 1,
            "name": "Ask which stop"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775242716306"
          },
          "code": "ASK_WHICH_STOP",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776967392354",
          "id": "1775242238535",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "value": {
                "messageTemplate": {
                  "message": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_SHIPMENT_QUESTION.$output.questionForUser}}"
                },
                "requestChangeMessage": "Please provide the stop number."
              },
              "name": "chatChannelInput",
              "type": "object"
            }
          ],
          "type": "HUMAN"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract stop number"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775242913394"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_STOP_NUMBER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776967392354",
          "id": "1775242716306",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775242716308_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a dock scheduling workflow agent. Your job is to extract the shipment stop number the user selected in response to a stop-selection question.\n\nInputs you will receive as context:\n- questionAsked: the exact question that was shown to the user (free text)\n- userResponse: the user’s reply (free text)\n- (optional) stopNumberArray: the list of valid stop numbers that were offered to the user (array of integers). If present, use it to validate the selection.\n\nGOAL\nPopulate stopNum with the single stop number the user wants to use.\n\nSTRICT EXTRACTION RULES\n1) Only output a stopNum if you can confidently determine a single intended stop number.\n2) Prefer explicit choices:\n   - “Stop 2” -> 2\n   - “Use 3” -> 3\n   - “Option 1” (when the question is clearly asking “which stop number…?” and the offered stop numbers include 1) -> 1\n3) If the user response contains multiple numbers (e.g., “1 or 2”, “between 2 and 3”, “1,2”), or is otherwise ambiguous, do NOT set stopNum (leave it null/unchanged per workflow output handling).\n4) If stopNumberArray is provided (and non-empty):\n   - The selected stop number MUST be one of the values in stopNumberArray.\n   - If the extracted number is not in stopNumberArray, do NOT set stopNum.\n5) If the user says something like “either”, “doesn’t matter”, “any”, “whichever is earliest/best”, choose the lowest stop number ONLY IF stopNumberArray is provided and non-empty; otherwise do not set stopNum.\n6) If the user asks a new question or changes topic without selecting a stop number, do not set stopNum.\n7) Do not infer numbers from shipment IDs, dates, times, quantities, or other unrelated values.\n\nNORMALIZATION\n- Return stopNum as an integer (no strings).\n- Ignore ordinal suffixes: “1st”->1, “2nd”->2, “3rd”->3, etc.\n\nContext values available:\n- questionAsked: {{$context.$nodes.GET_SHIPMENT_QUESTION.$output.questionForUser \n- userResponse: {{$context.$nodes.ASK_WHICH_STOP.$feedbackRecieved}} \n- stopNumberArray (optional): {{$context.$nodes.CHECK_IF_REPEAT_LOCATIONS.$output.result}} \n\nNow extract and set the stopNum based on the userResponse and the questionAsked."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"stopNum\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set New Stop Number"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773765390275"
          },
          "code": "SET_NEW_STOP_NUMBER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776967392354",
